The Container Yard – Lists, Tuples & Sets
​The Container Yard (Three Shapes, Three Jobs)
​LIST [ ] · THE PARTS BIN  
​Properties: Ordered, changeable, duplicates welcome.  
​Use Case: The default choice when things arrive, leave, and have positions.  
​Example: dias = [25.02, 24.98, 25.02] \rightarrow dias.append(25.10) \checkmark  
​TUPLE ( ) · THE SEALED RECORD  
​Properties: Ordered, frozen at creation.  
​Use Case: For things that must not drift: spec limits, calibration constants, a fixed (x, y) location.  
​Example: SPEC = (24.95, 25.05) \rightarrow SPEC[0] = 24.00 \boldsymbol{\times} (TypeError)  
​SET { } · THE NO-DUPLICATES BIN  
​Properties: Unordered, unique.  
​Use Case: Ask it "what distinct codes occurred?" or "is X in here?" and it answers instantly, however big it gets.  
​Example: codes = {"D01", "D07", "D01"} \rightarrow {"D01", "D07"} (duplicates gone)  
